==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]].
*4 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Golem Sunfish]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**8 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
**2 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.
**3 [[Zapy|Zapies]] spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is extremely dangerous due to the presence of Golem Sunfish which can render your anti-Zombie specialists useless with its 8-second curse that has full uptime, while the Surge Base forces you to play it safe and close to your own base. Zang Roo and Relic Doge's area attacks destroy small meatshields easily, leaving the Zapies to push with terrifying ease.

Try to eliminate the first wave of Relic Doges and the Zang Roo with disposable attackers before hitting the base. After which, you can max out your wallet without fear of enemies. Once at max cash, use a unit like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] to trigger the boss wave, then lure in the enemies out of the Surge Base's range.

Pushing too hard can actually be bad here, since you will eventually find yourself in the Surge Base's attacking range. Zapy acts as a wall that mostly prevents this from happening, but be wary of this fact while cleaning up the Zombies.

==Trivia==
*Both the English and Japanese names of Retreat of the Living Dead reference the film ''[[:wikipedia:The Return of the Living Dead|The Return of the Living Dead]].'' The name of the stage in the Japanese Version is pronounced similarly to ''Battalion'', the Japanese name of ''The Return of the Living Dead''. Through this, it can also be assumed that its name in the English Version is meant to reference the film's original English title.
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], the stage width was set to 4,800. The change was made because of a bug in how [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|Animated Bases]] spawn when not set as bosses.

